{
  "configuration_id": "config_014",
  "reason": "All 9 completed experiments use multiprofile, so the effect of profile setting (multiprofile vs singleprofile) is completely untested. The current best configuration (config_042: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, concat → 0.7150) strongly suggests that the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + concat combination is the most promising direction. config_014 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, singleprofile, None, concat) changes only the profile setting relative to config_042, making it a clean isolated comparison of whether multiprofile averaging actually contributes to the ~0.715 accuracy or whether a single profile is sufficient. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design question remaining: if singleprofile matches multiprofile, the pipeline is substantially simpler; if multiprofile is clearly superior, it validates the added complexity and focuses future effort on optimizing within the multiprofile space. Under a limited budget, resolving this fundamental axis before further tuning aggregation or fusion is the most efficient use of the next experiment."
}

